{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal","id":1011194,"title":"What happens if a vampire diablorizes an abyssal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-02T13:39:08-08:00","id":1011194,"title":"What happens if a vampire diablorizes an abyssal?","content":"I'm running a modern game, with vampires, but really we are going back to first edition of both vampire and exalted for this. Back when the general idea was that Exalted was the real history of the world of darkness and thus abyssals were the predecessors of vampires. It got me to thinking, then what would happen if a vampire tried to diablorize one? Nothing? Would they get a power boost? Would they explode? Become an abomination?<br /> <br /> This isn't like a question I expect there to be a solid answer I just thought it would be fun to discuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:43:32-08:00","id":1011196,"title":"","content":"I expect the soul of an Exalt isn't easy to digest. I'd take cue from when a high generation vampire diablorizes a low generation vampire. A power struggle for control over the vampire's body may take place. The vampire may experience moments where they can't account for their actions. (When the Exalt takes over). Depending on the power level and plot shenanigans, one will eventually over come the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:45:56-08:00","id":1011200,"title":"","content":"There's a Charcoal March of Spiders Charm that allows for a similar setup. Using on an Exalt with any kind of reincarnating Exaltation, however, makes the one who consumed it very sick for several days before the Exaltation leaves and goes about its normal business. So, probably that, but worse for the vampire. Didn't anyone ever tell you not to try eating an energy field larger than your head?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:53:14-08:00","id":1011204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011196#post1011196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect the soul of an Exalt isn't easy to digest. I'd take cue from when a high generation vampire diablorizes a low generation vampire. A power struggle for control over the vampire's body may take place. The vampire may experience moments where they can't account for their actions. (When the Exalt takes over). Depending on the power level and plot shenanigans, one will eventually over come the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to suggest something along this vein, essentially creating a &quot;persona&quot; in the vampire in the vein of the Ex3 Socialize Charms, modeled after the Abyssal, but placing its activation outside of the vampire's control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:22:58-08:00","id":1011219,"title":"","content":"A few other options:<br /> <br /> The vampire is affected by Whispers (Would the Neverborn be aspects of the Wyrm?)<br /> The Vampire is haunted by the ghost of the Abyssal. This may be a plus if the vampire was Giovanni.<br /> The Vampires memories are confused with the abyssal's. If the vampire sees someone the Abyssal knew, the vampire may go up to that person like they knew them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:56:37-08:00","id":1011234,"title":"","content":"There is also a matter of what happens to the exaltation. I'd default to it flying off but you could make the argument that diablorie takes the soul and thus the exaltation attached. Sure vampires are dead but they are also static at the moment of death like the abyssal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:01:29-08:00","id":1011235,"title":"","content":"There's also the fact that Abyssal Exaltations are still Solars somewhere underneath*, and Vampires really, REALLY don't like the sun.<br /> <br /> * though it'd also be valid to rule it out. Do what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:01:33-08:00","id":1011236,"title":"","content":"I like the idea the vampire turns into a walking Monstrosity for the Abyssal Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:25:45-08:00","id":1011245,"title":"","content":"Super-vampire, super-vampire, super-vampire!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:43:48-08:00","id":1011253,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I may be the boring guy here, but to diablerize something it has to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> If you drain all the blood from a human and keep on sucking you don't eat their soul, you just kill'em and act like people that suck on porkchop bones long after the meat is gone (people like me).<br /> <br /> Diablerie is a Blood calls to Blood thing. Not a generic soul sucking power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:51:10-08:00","id":1011256,"title":"","content":"Well yeah. But you could also point out vampires and exalts don't exist in the same setting. It's time to suspend your disbelief. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:58:06-08:00","id":1011259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011256#post1011256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah. But you could also point out vampires and exalts don't exist in the same setting. It's time to suspend your disbelief. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I get it is just a fun thing. But if I would mix cWoD and Exalted I wouldn't particularly do something like that.<br /> <br /> I just don't see these things meshing well enough to find a cool &quot;reason&quot; for why it would/should work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:04:58-08:00","id":1011261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011236#post1011236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea the vampire turns into a walking Monstrosity for the Abyssal Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh yea, there is that one mention that if there isn't a monstrance that the abyssal shard hides in dead bodies during the day, so maybe it hangs around until it finds someone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:09:04-08:00","id":1011263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Praise the Sun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011261#post1011261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> oh yea, there is that one mention that if there isn't a monstrance that the abyssal shard hides in dead bodies during the day, so maybe it hangs around until it finds someone</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampire kills someone. That someone Exalts as the Abyssal the vampire previously killed. Remembers the vampire killed their previous incarnation. <br /> <br /> That would be... awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:14:40-08:00","id":1011267,"title":"","content":"Depends on which soul they eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:33:48-08:00","id":1011274,"title":"","content":"Personally, I figure that if a vampire was in that situation, and drained an Abyssal to death, then nothing unusual would happen with regards to the Abyssal's reincarnation process. The really interesting bit would be that the vampire has drunk deeply of deathly Essence, creating a... what's that, Mr Vance? A super-vampire? Well, that sounds just dandy. A super-vampire. One that has gained new and nifty powers, and just a <i>huge</i> scoop of megalomania. <i>Things</i> whisper in his head, whispers of tearing it all down, and eternally ruling a realm of the dead...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:45:22-08:00","id":1011276,"title":"","content":"The same thing that happens if a vampire tires to kill a Solar or a Lunar or any other kind of Exalt. The vampire kills the Abyssal by sucking out all of his blood, the Abyssal's Exaltation flies free to find someone else to attach to and that's that.<br /> <br /> A more fun answer, though, might be allowing the vampire to permanently lower their generation by 1 point by at the same time have their &quot;lower soul&quot; awaken by brushing up against the undeath power of the Abyssals Exaltation. So the Vampire gets a lower generation but also has a Demon soul like the Kuei-jin do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:50:10-08:00","id":1011277,"title":"","content":"I had a Sidereal eat an abyssal's soul once(Charcoal March of Spiders). He picked up Whispers 5. Vomitted on someone else. Gave them some Whispers too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T20:33:08-08:00","id":1011333,"title":"","content":"Abyssal dies, vampire's head asplodes from Essence overload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T05:49:14-08:00","id":1011465,"title":"","content":"In your world, what happened in the intervening Ages such that Abyssals became Vampires? How does the relationship to Solars factor in? Is Golconda some remnant of Redemption? The &quot;best&quot; answer to your question is probably hidden in those details.<br /> <br /> <br /> And remember, the actual transformation from Age of Sorrows to World of Darkness has never been detailed. For example, Vampirism actually seems more similar to how Neverborn would imagine Terrestrial Exaltation; &quot;inherited&quot; by a corpse from its murderer. Maybe Abyssals aren't the proto-Vampires after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T06:50:25-08:00","id":1011482,"title":"","content":"If we're going by the theory diablerie can hold an exaltation with the vampire I'd say it turns into an impromptu exaltation. If said vampire wishes keep his new found power he will exalt as an abyssal, if he refuses he is permanently obliterated, for he stepped on the toes of oblivion and nothing survives contact with the void.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T08:58:13-08:00","id":1011521,"title":"","content":"Despite the common threads of blood drinking and relationship to death, I don't think Abyssals becoming vampires *directly* really works as far as stages of evolution go. The problem is that the Neverborn are such an essential element to what the Abyssal Exalted are, and, though my information may be outdated on this, I'm pretty sure the Neverborn are still playing their own dramatic role in the World of Darkness that doesn't really have anything to do with vampires specifically.<br /> <br /> That's not to say there can't be a thread (the assumption is that there is) but there were much more major changes than just &quot;looks like a vampire now.&quot;<br /> <br /> So a vampire who absorbs the Abyssal exaltation probably wouldn't just become a super-vampire, but rather something entirely new. Mixing magics is known to have strange effects, after all. But it would be more of a question for the World of Darkness books than the Exalted ones - who knows what happens when the Beast is suddenly tainted by Underworld Essence (and possibly subsumed by the Neverborn's psyche)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","user":"Remedy","date":". 12-03-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:38:21-08:00","id":1011562,"title":"","content":"You could have the vampire's lower soul awaken and give them access to appropriate spirit charms. Is the vampire in question about player or npc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:22:53-08:00","id":1011630,"title":"","content":"Hrm. Well, first this is just the opinion of some random dude on the internet, and I mean no disrespect to you or your game. But IMHO you're looking at this too superficially.<br /> <br /> Personally, I always thought that Exalted being the &quot;original history&quot; of the WoD was one of those internet myths that ran amok. Granted, we could see a fair bit of crossover from W;tA for the Lunar, but then again White Wolf's handling of the Lunar was shall we say in a modest effort at civility, ham fisted and clumsy. And yes, Abyssal's muck about with blood sacrifice and essence draining, but its only similar in the sense that frog legs taste like chicken.<br /> <br /> The Abyssals were not designed to be the vampires of Exalted, that line of thinking had its roots in some misguided fanboism of the vampire line of product. If anything Abyssals in a WoD relation was from the Wraith line. No seriously, it was. says so right in the front of the 1st edition book which I still own, it attributes most of it's inspiration to Wraith which the author felt was a &quot;vastly underrated game&quot; (I'll spare you my opinion on that matter). The only reason why blood was a thing, was because it was a form of sustenance to <i>all</i> the denizens of the Underworld, and the Abyssals were created under such vastly different conditions that any (IMHO) similarity between them is on the order of apples and walnuts. Case in point, Vampires have a say in creating their ersatz progeny and its been that way since Cain first got lonely way back when. Abyssals have no say in who inherits their divine shard, not even the Unconqured Sun has a say in it, they're a force of nature that seeks out a host by some set of metaphysics that is firmly seated in the concept of reincarnation, not familial inheritance.<br /> <br /> To be consistent you'd also have to answer the Lunar/Garou equation. Garou have kinfolk and both have genelogical purity ratings to breed future Garou because its a <i>genetic inheritance</i>. A Lunar, just like a Solar, has a divine shard that seeks out a host that &quot;is worthy&quot;. No genetics involved in the slightest bit. A Lunar can have 1000s of kids in their life time, and not a one of them becomes a Lunar because its all about the divine shard baby, not the little squiggly guy having a certain extra gene. Further, Lunar (1/2E admittedly, we don't know about 3E yet) gain the shapes of those who's hearts they ate. Garou don't. Can a Garou now eat the heart of a person and change into them? What about a Garou eating the heart of a Bastet? Can he now go AC/DC wolf/cat themes? How about Mages? Can they absorb the life force of another mage who mind you, is on a path of enlightened self discovery, and get a power up that way?<br /> <br /> But sticking with just vampires and Abysals. Abyssals are corrupted Solar shards, so suggesting a Vampire could drain a Abyssal and get anything other than a drug rush is to suggest they could do the same thing to Solars, Lunars, Sidereals, Exigents and Liminals. Doesn't add up.<br /> <br /> Personally, I never felt compelled to say that EX and WoD are the same continuity, they're each their own thing, with such vastly different metaphysics that trying to fuse them would (IMHO) result in a mess. But if I did, because a Abyssal is what he is, some fang succeeding at bleeding a Abyssal dry would only get a very powerful blood pool in his system, I'd let him use just 1 blood point for fueling disciplines at their maximum, or that they're at a +1 rating in potency, healing aggravated damage per day equal to his stamina, stuff like that. And he'd have a addiction for his troubles that he'd have to come to grips with or feed. A warlock would have some damn potent blood to do some pretty amazing rituals with and that's without drinking it himself as they'd be aware of the inherit dangers. <br /> <br /> In short, as Egon says, &quot;Don't cross the streams, bad things happen.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:55:23-08:00","id":1011680,"title":"","content":"Chiming in on the point Seeker made about the pre-history, what becomes what, etc.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Abyssals=Vampires, Solars=Imbued, Lunars=Werewolf&quot; was strictly a design space thing that was mentioned in The Making of Exalted. Kind of a &quot;If you like X, you'll probably dig Y.&quot;<br /> <br /> In Exalted-as-pre-history, the Abyssals didn't BECOME the vampires, they were the Age of Sorrows pulp fantasy splat that had a similar personal horror head-space. Hell, if you really want to get into a Timeline, Exalted pre-dates the Abrahamic God by an indeterminate amount of time, possibly an entire turn of the Cycle. Demon the Fallen really hard set a lot of the WoD's timeline. Vampires come from Caine, and did not exist prior.<br /> <br /> Assuming a vampire somehow actually managed to bite, drink, and drain an Abyssal, the most likely result would either be a finally dead Abyssal and the shard flying off to find a new host, or possibly just a really, really pissed Abyssal (depending on charm progression.) The vampire would likely be tripping balls and mad with power for a while, much like when they drink lupine, mage, changeling, etc blood, but nothing else. I'd argue that they couldn't even Embrace the Abyssal, since things like Risen, Mummies, etc cannot be embraced and an Abyssal is just a person who's death was stalled half way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:46:37-08:00","id":1011757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker1728</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011630#post1011630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm. Well, first this is just the opinion of some random dude on the internet, and I mean no disrespect to you or your game. But IMHO you're looking at this too superficially.<br /> <br /> Personally, I always thought that Exalted being the &quot;original history&quot; of the WoD was one of those internet myths that ran amok.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was planned in earlier development cycles and then scrapped by the time of the first edition core's release. At most, you saw some individuals advocating Thundarrism, but Thundarrists knew it wasn't official. The elseworlds thematic similarities, however, remain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted, we could see a fair bit of crossover from W;tA for the Lunar, but then again White Wolf's handling of the Lunar was shall we say in a modest effort at civility, ham fisted and clumsy. And yes, Abyssal's muck about with blood sacrifice and essence draining, but its only similar in the sense that frog legs taste like chicken. </div> </div> </div>The decision to use renown as an intricate status scoreboard still baffles me to this day. Like... how? Why? Who thought it would be a good idea? Lunars don't get their Charms from spirits that they have to impress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Abyssals were not designed to be the vampires of Exalted, that line of thinking had its roots in some misguided fanboism of the vampire line of product. </div> </div> </div>They are the vampires of Exalted, in that they have fangs, drink blood, and they have a gothic air to them that purposefully clashes with the wuxia and pop anime themes. The Fair Folk partially share this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anything Abyssals in a WoD relation was from the Wraith line. No seriously, it was. says so right in the front of the 1st edition book which I still own, it attributes most of it's inspiration to Wraith which the author felt was a &quot;vastly underrated game&quot; (I'll spare you my opinion on that matter). The only reason why blood was a thing, was because it was a form of sustenance to <i>all</i> the denizens of the Underworld, and the Abyssals were created under such vastly different conditions that any (IMHO) similarity between them is on the order of apples and walnuts. Case in point, Vampires have a say in creating their ersatz progeny and its been that way since Cain first got lonely way back when. Abyssals have no say in who inherits their divine shard, not even the Unconqured Sun has a say in it, they're a force of nature that seeks out a host by some set of metaphysics that is firmly seated in the concept of reincarnation, not familial inheritance. </div> </div> </div>The relation between the two is... confusing and unfortunate, as far as WW books goes, but it's kind of like a cleaned-up version of DSotBH before there was a V20 version of the Tal'Mahe'Ra book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be consistent you'd also have to answer the Lunar/Garou equation. Garou have kinfolk and both have genelogical purity ratings to breed future Garou because its a <i>genetic inheritance</i>. </div> </div> </div>(Gets out heavy stick)<br /> <br /> No, it's not genetic. It's purely spiritual heritage. Trying to base it on genes made it silly and more than a little ill-thought out. How the fuck do proteins allow you to violate the laws of physics? Especially if it's just one protein that's said to be recessive, which means that it's a trait that humans and wolves would have that's turned off in Garou...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Lunar, just like a Solar, has a divine shard that seeks out a host that &quot;is worthy&quot;. No genetics involved in the slightest bit. A Lunar can have 1000s of kids in their life time, and not a one of them becomes a Lunar because its all about the divine shard baby, not the little squiggly guy having a certain extra gene. Further, Lunar (1/2E admittedly, we don't know about 3E yet) gain the shapes of those who's hearts they ate. Garou don't. </div> </div> </div>Again, it's an elseworlds head-tilt kind of thing. A lot of the aims and themes of Werewolf live in Lunars. The Lunars are, of course, a vastly different take on bestial shapeshifters fighting back against a ruling order that's trying to kill them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a Garou now eat the heart of a person and change into them? </div> </div> </div>They don't need to; there's a Gift that just allows them to duplicate someone's appearance, called, appropriately enough, Doppelganger (or Monkey's Uncle, if you're a Bastet and have to ice skate up hill)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about a Garou eating the heart of a Bastet? Can he now go AC/DC wolf/cat themes? </div> </div> </div>In line with the above, there's actually a Gift supplied by a moon Incarna that allows any changer that learns it to turn into a cat. Botching it strands Garou halfway between being a wolf and a cat.<br /> <br /> Or you could just be called Jay No Name and not need to do that, either. (Glares at early W:tA fiction)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about Mages? Can they absorb the life force of another mage who mind you, is on a path of enlightened self discovery, and get a power up that way? </div> </div> </div>You're going a bit off the rails here. Mages are Sidereal-likes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But sticking with just vampires and Abysals. Abyssals are corrupted Solar shards, so suggesting a Vampire could drain a Abyssal and get anything other than a drug rush is to suggest they could do the same thing to Solars, Lunars, Sidereals, Exigents and Liminals. Doesn't add up. </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be the first time Vampire had nonsensical rules about blood and trait boosting. Remember Werewolf Pure Breed? It's a strictly social advantage, which conveys no additional power. For some reason, Kindred that drink blood from Garou or Fera that have it gain physical Discipline boosts. And that isn't even the worst thought-out crossover rule between the two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I never felt compelled to say that EX and WoD are the same continuity, they're each their own thing, with such vastly different metaphysics that trying to fuse them would (IMHO) result in a mess. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if I did, because a Abyssal is what he is, some fang succeeding at bleeding a Abyssal dry would only get a very powerful blood pool in his system, I'd let him use just 1 blood point for fueling disciplines at their maximum, or that they're at a +1 rating in potency, healing aggravated damage per day equal to his stamina, stuff like that. And he'd have a addiction for his troubles that he'd have to come to grips with or feed. A warlock would have some damn potent blood to do some pretty amazing rituals with and that's without drinking it himself as they'd be aware of the inherit dangers.<br /> <br /> In short, as Egon says, &quot;Don't cross the streams, bad things happen.&quot;<br /> </div> </div> </div>You might get a result like one of the Hungry Dead getting Golden Cycled from Yugen taken from the little gods. They can make leaps and bounds in transcending their prior limits... until they run out of Yugen, at which point all those gains go up in smoke and they're back where they started. Suicide into Final Death often follows that crash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Demon the Fallen really hard set a lot of the WoD's timeline. Vampires come from Caine, and did not exist prior.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Demon didn't fix anything (haha! multiple entendres!). Every game has its run-down of events that preceded everything, and all the other games tend to completely ignore it. Demon is in the same boat; its explanation of reality and time only holds if you're playing Demon. Other games continue to ignore it and do their own thing. I mean, before W20, Werewolf didn't even divy up the Umbra the same way that Mage does, and still doesn't, because Werewolf, like other WoD settings that aren't Mage, doesn't assume that space is a part of the spirit world. Demon is going to work out with everything else the same way; the layers of reality explanation is basically just about the same as Mage's need to filter everything through its attempts to make unified magic(k)al theory, right down to how many fucks other games give about it (spoiler, the answer is 0 fucks).</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:47:15-08:00","id":1011758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011521#post1011521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite the common threads of blood drinking and relationship to death\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>And immortality, and Abyssals being able to take Charms to remove their ability to eat food, and Abyssals can take Charms to turn off their vital functions, and Abyssals can take Charms to take shelter inside the bosom of the earth, and Abyssals can take Charms to hide from the mind's eyes of other people, and how some Abyssals become supernaturally ugly with Appearance 0, and\u2026<br /> <br /> I could keep going. I'm surprised Abyssals didn't get aura-reading or Dementation.<br /> <br /> That said, there's thousands of years' worth of space for the transition to be made more slowly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011521#post1011521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the Neverborn are such an essential element to what the Abyssal Exalted are\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta disagree with you there. There are some links, true, but I bet I could cut the Neverborn entirely out of my current Exalted game without it even getting noticed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011521#post1011521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a vampire who absorbs the Abyssal exaltation probably wouldn't just become a super-vampire, but rather something entirely new.</div> </div> </div> </div>A &quot;super-vampire&quot; <i>is</i> something new. Well, rather, new to the World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> Guess it depends on your definition of &quot;super-vampire,&quot; really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T19:02:47-08:00","id":1011784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011758#post1011758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And immortality, and Abyssals being able to take Charms to remove their ability to eat food, and Abyssals can take Charms to turn off their vital functions</div> </div> </div> </div>This all sort of falls under the general semi-undead banner, so while they do have it in <i>common</i>, I don't consider it especially Vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , and Abyssals can take Charms to take shelter inside the bosom of the earth, and Abyssals can take Charms to hide from the mind's eyes of other people </div> </div> </div>... Okay, fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , and how some Abyssals become supernaturally ugly with Appearance 0, and\u2026 </div> </div> </div>See first response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could keep going. I'm surprised Abyssals didn't get aura-reading or Dementation. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how they'd fit thematically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, there's thousands of years' worth of space for the transition to be made more slowly. </div> </div> </div>Well, certainly. I'd expect no less lengthy a process for an Exaltation to turn into something you can bite into people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I gotta disagree with you there. There are some links, true, but I bet I could cut the Neverborn entirely out of my current Exalted game without it even getting noticed. </div> </div> </div>Not that this is a bad thing, but I feel we have a pretty different interpretation of the Exalted setting. I see the Neverborn as one of the primary forces in the overall setting, and as having a significant amount of influence on their Abyssal underlings (even disregarding the large amount of indirect influence fostered through their correspondence with the Deathlords, who serve as the immediate bosses of the deathknights) and on the ghost-related parts of Creation such as Shadowlands and, well, ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A &quot;super-vampire&quot; <i>is</i> something new. Well, rather, new to the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>Okay, fair enough. I still think it would be something a bit more evocative and exotic than what &quot;super-vampire&quot; brings to mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Guess it depends on your definition of &quot;super-vampire,&quot; really. </div> </div> </div>Or this, yeah, I like how you said it better actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T19:21:30-08:00","id":1011787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011784#post1011784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how they'd fit thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, there are Charms for shredding sanity in the Abyssal Manual, and it wouldn't be much of a stretch for Through Dead Eyes or the like to reveal the glow of the living. Just a thought.<br /> <br /> (Also, there was a Deathlord to match each clan)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not that this is a bad thing, but I feel we have a pretty different interpretation of the Exalted setting. I see the Neverborn as one of the primary forces in the overall setting, and as having a significant amount of influence on their Abyssal underlings (even disregarding the large amount of indirect influence fostered through their correspondence with the Deathlords, who serve as the immediate bosses of the deathknights) and on the ghost-related parts of Creation such as Shadowlands and, well, ghosts. </div> </div> </div>1e went rather far to sell the Neverborn as the ultimate antagonists, and 2e took out the limiter. This knocked off the course of several books' subject matters and led to a more villainous than thou competition with the later-arriving Infernals that made the setting go even further afield. As such, EX3 tends to hearken to the setup of the first edition STC's presentation of the Deathlords and Abyssals, where they likely have nothing inherently to do with the Neverborn and don't want to kill the living and then kill the dead, except where it might specifically benefit the schemes of an Abyssal or their liege in the Underworld. Usually, this has to do with purely political maneuvering, rather than being a cult leader to non-existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T19:30:42-08:00","id":1011790,"title":"","content":"<b>What happens if a vampire diablorizes an abyssal?</b><br /><br />The vampire in question would become a gothic god of death, dwarfing any vampire in the whole history of the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even if said vampire only equates to being as &quot;powerful&quot; as an abyssal half-caste. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:57:38-08:00","id":1012151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1011757#post1011757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Gets out heavy stick)<br /> <br /> No, it's not genetic. It's purely spiritual heritage. Trying to base it on genes made it silly and more than a little ill-thought out. How the fuck do proteins allow you to violate the laws of physics? Especially if it's just one protein that's said to be recessive, which means that it's a trait that humans and wolves would have that's turned off in Garou...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the lengthy reply Saur Ops, got a chuckle from that above as that was the exact same discussion I had with my group back in the late 90s when I was running W;tA. I cut the rest of your reply out not because I didn't want to engage, because in fact I'd have a real sense of pleasure in exchanging thoughts and info based on your reply, but I came to realize something reading this and that other thread regarding WW's survey. I've been out of touch with the WoD product line for some time now, going on 15 years. I kept my interest in Exalted because there was a small group here in Vegas that was still into it, but that group dissolved after a short period and left me to mostly GM via the net with a couple of old college buddies who had no interest in any WoD products. And as a result, i didn't buy any of the books either.<br /> <br /> So in short, in respect to the OP's question, I have to apologize and say that apparently there was some kind of decision to say EX's world was the precursor to the WoD that I totally missed. And I stand by the original point...what a hot mess of a idea that is, I'll remain (somewhat) civil and refrain from being overly caustic towards the pitcher of that idea other than to say it is beyond stupid IMHO <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":12415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","user":"Seeker1728","date":". 12-04-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:10:50-08:00","id":1012203,"title":"","content":"Wow this moved alot faster than I thought. I was expecting maybe three or four posts not 15. To answer a few questions.<br /> <br /> First off, I didn't have Exalted as the real history of WoD because I thought it was true or even a good idea. In fact I've done the opposite and made tweaks in WoD to better fit that ideal. My motivation was that WoD would give some low level stuff for them to deal with and could easily be brushed aside when the game reaches a certain level. The power scale and d10 system of WoD made it easy to rules hack into the game. I cannot go into detail because figuring out how the world became what it is is part of the mystery of the game and half the group frequents here. If you are curious I'll list what they do know. Putting it in a dropdown so its easy to skip if you dont<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">-Some point long before the world became as you know it the abyssal exalted were imprisoned in individual tombs that are now scattered over the Earth. The first one that the players were aware of was discovered by a vampire cult, she claimed to be Cain and took over but they found out her true identity as powerful abyssal specializing in necrotech and social manipulation. Once they found a still comatose abyssal who was revived when given essence, a third regained consciousness while still trapped and has lost their mind from the trauma. The solars imprisoned the abyssals along with the help of someone the abyssals simply refer to as &quot;the traitor&quot;<br /> <br /> -The Great Maker died. His corpse forms the ceiling of the underworld leaving it sandwiched between layers of labyrinth. Alchemical exalted eventually went extinct as well<br /> <br /> -About 100,000 years ago the world as we know it was created. The incarna still exist but effectively gone from the world. At times prayers are still answered by them however<br /> <br /> -Malfeas and Yu Shan exist but were sealed off from the world. If any demons or gods know how or why they aren't talking.<br /> <br /> -Lunars originally only appeared among werewolves, thats no longer true<br /> <br /> -Although hard to place approximate times all celestial exalted resurfaced around the same time<br /> <br /> -Dragonbloods still exist but are so watered down Earth only sees one every century or so.<br /> <br /> -Arcane fate and the great curse are both gone<br /> <br /> -Hunters are not solars, but they have noticed similarities<br /> <br /> -The white veil society, or something similar, still doesn't exist</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So everyone knows. I did not allow players to be vampires or abyssals in this game. If this occurred it would be strictly npc to npc. For that reason, honestly I'd do whatever made the story more interesting. This wasn't for some hard ruling. Its just an idea I was toying with and wanted to share it for fun. See what pops into people's heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:01:10-08:00","id":1012300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Praise the Sun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1012203#post1012203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The Great Maker died. His corpse forms the ceiling of the underworld leaving it sandwiched between layers of labyrinth. Alchemical exalted eventually went extinct as well</div> </div> </div> </div>Autochthonia is actually a place in the deep Umbra that is now the base of Iteration X in MtA. Now, if you're going for pre-history, there's plenty of play there. The Autochthonia that is now inhabited by ItX is the dead husk of the great maker, the great maker is alive and well and directs ItX, or the great maker continues to slumber away and the ItX are interacting with the Divine Ministers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:21:49-08:00","id":1012508,"title":"","content":"The Kindred's head blows up? Nothing really interesting? I mean, the power of an Exalt lies not within his SOUL but the Exalted Shard stuffed in there. When an Exalt dies, it takes off and nothing short of, basically, Cosmic powers, are going to keep it there. If you want a canon answer, however, and you're using Exalted as Pre-WoD (as well you should but we won't get into that) then just look at what happens when a Kindred tries to do the same to a Hunter. HINT: Nothing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T17:35:18-08:00","id":1012885,"title":"","content":"I thought hunter blood was toxic to vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7554-praise-the-sun","name":"Praise the Sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T17:43:51-08:00","id":1012891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Praise the Sun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1011194-what-happens-if-a-vampire-diablorizes-an-abyssal?p=1012885#post1012885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought hunter blood was toxic to vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>While there might be an edge to do that, as a rule, no, it is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}